{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "note": "Centrelines for the five modelled links, derived from OpenStreetMap way geometry (Gardiner Expressway, Lake Shore Boulevard West, The Queensway). A divided road is two carriageways in OSM, so the points are binned by longitude and the median latitude of each bin is taken, which collapses them onto one line. The eastern links begin exactly where the western ones end so the corridor is continuous at the Humber. Presentation only: nothing in the model reads these coordinates. They replace hand-digitised alignments sitting 226-441 m from the real roads on average and 781 m at worst, which drew the corridor over open water in Humber Bay.",
